<title>SPAIN: Spanish Treasury sets November auction volumes.</title>
<headline>Spanish Treasury sets November auction volumes.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain announced on Monday the amount of notes and bonds the Spanish Treasury would tender at its monthly auctions on Tuesday and Wednesday.</p>
<p>Following are the minimum and maximum amounts:</p>
<p>(billion pesetas)</p>
<p>    DAY			   from		 to</p>
<p>    5/11 (3- and 10-year)    275		 325</p>
<p>    6/11 (5- and 15-year)    150		 200</p>
<p>    October auctions	 amount announced   allotted</p>
<p>    1/10 (3- and 10-year)	275 - 325	357 *</p>
<p>    2/10 (5- and 15-year)	200 - 250	244 *</p>
<p>* This is the amount actually sold on the market and includes the second segment of the auction.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
